// GENERATED from a VU1 EFU sweep on real PS2 hardware (SCPH-90000 over
// ps2link). Do not edit by hand.
//
// EATANxy rows are built so the range reduction is exact: with x = 1-d and
// y = 1+d the adder masks nothing, y-x is 2d and x+y is 2, so the reduced
// argument is d and none of it rests on the divider. DYAD walks d over the
// powers of two, which is where the adder's guard mask reads the leading
// coefficient out one bit at a time; GRD* step d linearly; NEAR drives the
// reduced argument towards +-1. EEXP and ESIN take their argument straight.
